# Fibonacci / Additive-Basis / Farey Bridge Scout

## Fibonacci Rows
Identity: F_n = sum_k binom(n-k-1,k).
For n>=2 this is the rank vector of independent sets in path P_{n-2}.

n= 1 F_n=  1 row=1                  zeck(F_n)=[1]
n= 2 F_n=  1 row=1                  zeck(F_n)=[1]
n= 3 F_n=  2 row=1+1                zeck(F_n)=[2]
n= 4 F_n=  3 row=1+2                zeck(F_n)=[3]
n= 5 F_n=  5 row=1+3+1              zeck(F_n)=[5]
n= 6 F_n=  8 row=1+4+3              zeck(F_n)=[8]
n= 7 F_n= 13 row=1+5+6+1            zeck(F_n)=[13]
n= 8 F_n= 21 row=1+6+10+4           zeck(F_n)=[21]
n= 9 F_n= 34 row=1+7+15+10+1        zeck(F_n)=[34]
n=10 F_n= 55 row=1+8+21+20+5        zeck(F_n)=[55]
n=11 F_n= 89 row=1+9+28+35+15+1     zeck(F_n)=[89]

